Mutant: nov-unsub-dying-throws-230
Kind: bug
Since: 2.3.0
Version-note: the 2.3.0 API (Filter.ReservedCount from the types, World.UnsubscribeLater); older trees have nothing to break
Class: same class, new place (2.3.0: World.UnsubscribeLater; the W6 class: a KENSEI_DEBUG check)
Configs: dbg
Expect: defect unsub-later:dying-entity repro-verified
Why: under KENSEI_DEBUG UnsubscribeLater checks IsAlive instead of alive-or-dying: a listener that leaves while its entity's own DestroyEntity runs throws
Not-rel: release does not check the entity

diff --git a/KenseiECS/Core/WorldListenerExtensions.cs b/KenseiECS/Core/WorldListenerExtensions.cs
--- a/KenseiECS/Core/WorldListenerExtensions.cs
+++ b/KenseiECS/Core/WorldListenerExtensions.cs
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@
                 return;
             }
 #if KENSEI_DEBUG
-            if (!world.IsAliveOrDying(entity)) {
+            if (!world.IsAlive(entity)) {
                 throw new InvalidOperationException($"UnsubscribeLater<{typeof(T).Name}>: entity {entity} is not alive");
             }
 #endif
